<section class="pt-12 pb-10 sm:pt-16 sm:pb-12 px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <!-- Opening Statement -->
  <div class="space-y-5">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.1] text-ink max-w-[24ch]">
      <span class="text-accent">OmniBuf:</span> a fast,{' '}
      <span class="whitespace-nowrap">self-describing</span> wire format
    </h1>

    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[65ch]">
      OmniBuf is a faster and more expressive binary serialization format for <code>.proto</code>{' '}
      files or plain structs with simple annotations. Most of Protobuf is great: schemas, explicit
      field numbers, gRPC, Connect. OmniBuf just replaces the wire format underneath. Packets encode
      and decode faster, and raw <code>.obuf</code> bytes dump straight to JSON when the schema
      isn't around.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 pt-1 text-sm">
      <a href="/how-it-works" class="btn-primary px-4 py-2">
        How It Works &rarr;
      </a>
      <a href="/spec" class="btn-secondary px-4 py-2">
        Wire Specification
      </a>
      <a href="/benchmarks" class="btn-secondary px-4 py-2">
        Benchmarks
      </a>
      <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink/65 sm:ml-2">v1 DRAFT-1</span>
    </div>
  </div>

